      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & f(x)=\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{3}{x}+3, x \\neq 0 \\\\ & f^{\\prime}(x)=\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{3}{x^2}=0 \\quad \\Rightarrow x= \\pm 3 \\\\ & f^{\\prime}(x)=\\frac{x^2-3}{3 x^2}\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}(\\mathrm{x}) \\gt 0 \\forall(-\\infty,-3) \\cup(3, \\infty) \\rightarrow \\text { increasing } \\\\ & \\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}(\\mathrm{x}) \\lt 0 \\forall(-3,0) \\cup(0,3) \\rightarrow \\text { decreasing }\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\sum_{i=1}^5 \\alpha_i^2=(-3)^2+(3)^2+(-3)^2+(0)^2+(3)^2$<br/>$=36$",
    "image": null
  },
